{
  "version": 1,
  "description": "Sealed operations x25519-xc20p-seal (spec §3.6), sealed to seal_pub[e] of seal-key.json seal_keys (vault shared). epk = X25519(ephemeral_secret, 9); shared = X25519(ephemeral_secret, seal_pub) (all-zero: bad_request); seal_key = HKDF-SHA256(ikm=shared, salt=epk || seal_pub, info=utf8(\"akv1/seal\"), L=32); aad = cjson({\"ctx\":\"akv1/sealed-op\",\"vault_id\",\"sealed_id\",\"key_epoch\",\"origin\",\"ts\"}); ct = XChaCha20-Poly1305(seal_key, n, cjson(op), aad). cases: sealOp with the given ephemeral_secret, nonce wire.n and sealed_id MUST reproduce wire byte for byte, and openSealedOp(SealSK[key_epoch], wire, {vault_id}) MUST yield op. openSealedOp order: parse (v or alg unknown: unsupported_version; exact keys, IDs, epk 32 B, n 24 B, ct 16..65552 B, origin {kind \"mcp\", account 1..256, client_id 1..256 and grant_id 1..64 printable ASCII}, ts: bad_request); vault_id other than expected (bad_request); all-zero shared secret (bad_request); AEAD failure (decrypt_failed); pt not canonical, unknown op, set without value, delete with value or sensitivity, unknown keys (bad_request). invalid: open the wire with SealSK of open_with_epoch and MUST fail with expect_error; a wire with ct_zero_bytes replaces ct with b64 of that many zero bytes. seal_invalid: sealOp MUST refuse op with expect_error (an op with value_fill uses value = value_fill repeated value_length times). drain: opened = openSealedOp(SealSK[drain.wire.key_epoch], drain.wire, {vault_id: drain.wire.vault_id}); checkSealedDrain(opened, {account, now, sealed_ttl_s, seen}) takes only that authenticated result, in order: origin.account other than account (forbidden); sealed_id in seen, a replay (conflict); now - ts > sealed_ttl_s * 1000 (bad_request); ts - now > 300000 (bad_request). drain.cases MUST pass; drain.invalid MUST fail with expect_error.",
